WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.720
It seemed that The Foundation was all but rid of&nbsp;
SCP-682 after an unlikely glitch in reality sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.960
the hard-to-destroy reptile deep into a limitless&nbsp;
interdimensional abyss known simply as The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:19.320
Backrooms. This meant that the standard reality,&nbsp;
also known as The Frontrooms, was safe from one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.840
the most dangerous monsters in existence, but&nbsp;
that didn’t mean the anomaly was neutralized.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:30.000
SCP-682 had been slowly but surely&nbsp;
making its way through every level of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.980
The Backrooms and taking out its aggression&nbsp;
on any living thing that crossed its path.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.960
Well, except for Jerry. There was something&nbsp;
about the entity which resembled blue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:46.440
hyacinth macaw that had made it tolerable&nbsp;
to SCP-682, which was rare for the reptile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:52.800
as it infamously regarded most other lifeforms&nbsp;
as disgusting and worthy only to be destroyed.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.960
Jerry had been frightened away by an encounter&nbsp;
with the archers of Level 10, and ever since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:03.840
SCP-682 had been looking for the little guy.&nbsp;
This search eventually led the creature to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:10.680
backtrack through the suburbs of Level 9 and&nbsp;
enter Level 11: the “presumably” infinite city.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:16.200
This was the largest settlement that&nbsp;
SCP-682 had seen in The Backrooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:22.380
and whether or not it found its avian companion,&nbsp;
it was eager to cause some havoc among the locals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:28.380
And speaking of the locals, what a sorry sight&nbsp;
they were. Countless Facelings were acting like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:33.300
ordinary humans going about their day, strolling&nbsp;
down the sidewalks and entering buildings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:39.180
seemingly with no reason other than to humor&nbsp;
the themed environment. A few of the Facelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.400
were even walking Hounds on leashes, in&nbsp;
a grotesque pantomime of a dog walker.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:51.420
682 was infuriated. Somehow, in its seemingly&nbsp;
infinite ways of causing the creature distress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.200
The Backrooms had managed to combine&nbsp;
the two things that annoyed it most:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.420
the so-called “civilized” creatures of its&nbsp;
native reality and the equally disgusting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.940
entities that dwelled within The Backrooms.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:09.660
Unable to stand to look at this any longer,&nbsp;
SCP-682 went on a violent rampage, attacking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:14.700
every entity in sight. Its previous objective&nbsp;
of seeking Jerry no longer mattered to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.920
as the anomaly’s disgust for every part of&nbsp;
this alternate reality overwhelmed all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.300
its thoughts. If 682 found itself&nbsp;
starring in Pixar’s Inside Out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.860
all of the emotions in its mind&nbsp;
would be variations of disgust.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:34.980
As the bodies started to pile up, SCP-682&nbsp;
began to sense something in the air waves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:40.320
of this Level. It soon adapted a long-range&nbsp;
radio antenna in order to better pick up on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.420
frequency. The voice on the other was calm,&nbsp;
and sounded like a middle-aged human male.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:51.060
“You’re listening to Radio Backrooms.” The&nbsp;
voice said. “If you’re just tuning in now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.780
welcome to Talkin’ With&nbsp;
Ralph. I’m your host, Ralph!”

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:01.680
There you are. SCP-682 said, triangulating&nbsp;
the radio signal with its internal senses.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:08.700
This “Ralph” character was going to be next to&nbsp;
die. Well, he’d be next if nothing else with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.680
dumb look about it got in the way. And in The&nbsp;
Backrooms, the chances were high that a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:19.380
pathetic creature for SCP-682 to destroy&nbsp;
would be around every corner. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:25.200
682 marked the new waypoint on its mental map&nbsp;
and started to zero in on Ralph’s location.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.000
“Looks like we’ve got ourselves a brand&nbsp;
new entity in Level 11.” Ralph’s voice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.960
echoed in SCP-682’s skull. “I’ll be giving away a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.100
free time slot to whichever faction bags&nbsp;
the beast within the next twelve hours.”

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:44.700
SCP-682 realized almost immediately that it must&nbsp;
have been the new entity that Ralph was referring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.860
to. It was familiar with the idea of factions&nbsp;
within The Backrooms because of its previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:56.040
encounters with the Major Explorer Group, but now&nbsp;
the situation threatened to get interesting. Maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.480
there would be some factions here with actual&nbsp;
combat training on par with the mobile task&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.940
forces. Could these new factions pose a&nbsp;
challenge to such a powerful keter-class anomaly?

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:09.120
682 heard the buzzing of&nbsp;
tiny propellers overheard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.860
and saw a group of surveillance drones&nbsp;
flying towards it. With catlike agility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:19.440
it leaped into the air and swatted the drones&nbsp;
with its limbs and claws. The cheap hunks of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:24.480
carbon fiber were shattered easily. Halfway&nbsp;
across the city, several members of The Drone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.080
Surveillance Squad were throwing their&nbsp;
headsets on the ground in frustration.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.480
With one faction having missed its chance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.940
the next was quick to arrive. Five cool&nbsp;
teens on bikes and skateboards rolled up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.960
to the end of the street. They were all&nbsp;
dressed in 80s fashion, for some reason.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:45.240
“Check it out! That’s one righteous&nbsp;
reptile!” said one of the teens.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.400
“Gnarly!” said another.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:52.560
682 cringed. Even with its limited&nbsp;
understanding of human culture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.600
it could tell that 80s nostalgia was&nbsp;
overplayed, and that the era of 90s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.160
and 2000s nostalgia would soon arrive.&nbsp;
And what better way to hasten it than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.600
getting these troubled teens off the street.&nbsp;
Just don’t ask where they went after that.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:12.720
Another so-called faction down and SCP-682&nbsp;
was already feeling uncontested. So far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:18.060
these humans were even less intimidating than&nbsp;
the entities. This was a bit mind-boggling to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:23.580
SCP-682 considering that the Foundation was&nbsp;
made up of humans and they had managed to bag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:30.240
several much scarier anomalies than anything&nbsp;
in The Backrooms. Naturally, SCP-682 included&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:35.340
itself among that number. The radio studio where&nbsp;
Talkin’ with Ralph was broadcasting from was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:41.220
getting ever closer. Taking a slight detour, the&nbsp;
reptile tore straight through Level 11’s M.E.G.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:46.380
base of operations. Once again, the explorers&nbsp;
within proved to be no match for the creature.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.400
It emerged out the other side of the&nbsp;
building, back into the city streets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:55.800
and was immediately confronted with several&nbsp;
new explorers. These humans weren’t exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:00.720
80s fashionable, opting instead for&nbsp;
tactical gear and long black cloaks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.040
They had a haunted look about them&nbsp;
and each carried a mighty spear.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:10.080
“Sinner!” They shouted in unison.&nbsp;
“The eyes of Argos are upon you!”

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:16.020
SCP-682 pounced and made short work of them,&nbsp;
but paused warily when it noticed the presence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:21.060
of a slightly taller humanoid that had been&nbsp;
standing behind the group. It was dressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:26.880
the same as the humans, but it had an aura&nbsp;
of mythic fury. The humanoid had no eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:33.840
but somehow, SCP-682 could feel itself&nbsp;
being watched, as if from all places at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:39.180
once. It was unsettling for the creature, as&nbsp;
it felt like being back at the Foundation.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:44.880
Contained in a vat of acid while a science lab&nbsp;
full of researchers watched and judged. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:50.940
judged. That was the feeling.&nbsp;
And SCP-682 knew it all too well.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.880
The humanoid stepped forward,&nbsp;
brandishing its spear.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:59.220
What was it with this place&nbsp;
and spears? SCP-682 wondered.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.780
The powerful entity it had fought on&nbsp;
Level 7 had also wielded a spear. Was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:07.440
that weapon meant to be some indication&nbsp;
that this one was just as tough?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:15.000
“I am all-seeing Argos, and I have seen that your&nbsp;
sins are innumerable!” said the humanoid entity.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:21.600
Argos lunged forward, thrusting with its spear&nbsp;
towards 682. The reptile received the brunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:26.580
of the strike and was launched backward.&nbsp;
Without even giving 682 time to recover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:31.020
Argos thrust its spear through the&nbsp;
creature, pinning it to the concrete.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:37.620
“Sinners must be punished!” Argos bellowed,&nbsp;
pushing the spear deeper into the reptile’s body.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:44.340
SCP-682 struck back with a bite, but to its&nbsp;
surprise, Argos seemed to have an impossibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:49.800
high tolerance for pain and its wounds seemed to&nbsp;
be healing almost as soon as they opened. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:55.080
told 682 that close-range attacks wouldn’t get&nbsp;
this entity’s spear out of its back. It needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:00.540
to get the freaky humanoid out of spear range,&nbsp;
and then hit back with a reach weapon of its own.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:07.560
Tapping once again into the radio frequencies,&nbsp;
682 levied a blast of concussive sonic energy from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:13.080
its body. While this didn’t damage Argos, it did&nbsp;
achieve the intended effect of knocking the entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:19.680
a few feet back. SCP-682 used this chance to get&nbsp;
a bit of distance, and readied its next weapon:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:25.140
its own reptilian tail, now-elongated and&nbsp;
equipped with a sharp blade at the end.&nbsp;

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:31.740
In terms of reach, SCP-682’s tail whip&nbsp;
outclassed Argos’ spear. The battle was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:36.840
on now. 682 swung its powerful blade in an&nbsp;
attempt to cut through the enemy's weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.520
but it seemed that the spear had the same&nbsp;
regenerative abilities as its wielder.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:47.820
“You’re not human.” SCP-682 taunted&nbsp;
Argos. “You’re even more disgusting!”

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.940
“You are a sinner!” Argos replied.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:56.460
Regeneration was one of SCP-682’s strong&nbsp;
suits too, and the spear wounds that Argos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:00.540
had given it had already recovered.&nbsp;
Using the bladed-whip of its tail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:07.080
SCP-682 kept Argos and his spear out of&nbsp;
close-quarters. It continued to slash the entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:11.760
but the wounds were healing too quickly&nbsp;
to leave an impression. Argos was also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:16.560
skilled enough with his spear that he began&nbsp;
to deflect the whip and advance towards 682.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:24.300
It was time to try something crazy. So crazy it&nbsp;
just might work. Argos stopped in his tracks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:31.020
as suddenly SCP-682 was nowhere to be found.&nbsp;
The reptile had become effectively invisible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:37.140
and this was because it had adapted to counter&nbsp;
Argos’ “true vision.” Now encased in a ghostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:43.860
aura of sin-cloaking energy, SCP-682 maneuvered&nbsp;
around Argos and prepared to finish it off.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:51.900
If you’re like me, then this won’t bring you down.&nbsp;
But it will hurt, Argos, and I will enjoy it.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:55.320
Calling upon the memories of the&nbsp;
acid vats back at the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.320 --> 00:10:01.800
SCP-682 secreted a powerful acid across&nbsp;
its entire body and leapt onto Argos’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:06.540
back. The thing about spears is, while they are&nbsp;
ideal for engaging the opponent at a distance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:12.180
they were far less useful if that same opponent&nbsp;
was grappling your limbs. With his weapon rendered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:18.600
unusable, Argos was now locked in a battle of&nbsp;
endurance with SCP-682 - it had generated the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:23.520
most powerful acid it could generate, potent&nbsp;
enough to even cause a bit of damage to itself.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:30.900
“It’s over, Argos.” SCP-682 chuckled. “You&nbsp;
may be good at fighting, but only one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:36.360
us has spent years being contained&nbsp;
within a caustic prison. You lose.”

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:43.740
SCP-682 held down Argos for as long as it took for&nbsp;
the acid to fully immobilize him. The entity had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:49.080
struggled to break free, but 682 was able to&nbsp;
continually grow strong enough to tighten its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:55.160
grip. With the boss of this level destroyed,&nbsp;
SCP-682 continued towards the radio tower.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:11:01.260
“Uhh… umm…. Congratulations, you!”&nbsp;
Ralph said over the radio. “You win,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:06.000
lizard man. How about you and&nbsp;
I have a nice, peaceful chat.”

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.440
Not having any of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:12.720
SCP-682 beamed its own words into the&nbsp;
radio station along the same frequency.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:15.000
“Tell me how to get to the next level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:20.040
and I’ll consider sparing you. But only&nbsp;
because you’re just that worthless.”

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:24.420
“I hear ya, lizard man!”&nbsp;
Ralph responded, nervously.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:30.300
Ralph directed SCP-682 to a specific window&nbsp;
inside of one of the nearby skyscrapers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:35.400
When SCP-682 opened this window, it&nbsp;
was immediately transported into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:39.060
cramped white room with a table&nbsp;
that had a single chair nearby.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.100
This was Level 12?

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:46.860
682 was most assuredly going back&nbsp;
for Ralph later. Yet another level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:50.760
seemed specifically created to play&nbsp;
on the ennui of the human condition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:54.600
which was something that 682 still&nbsp;
had no frame of reference for.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:59.520
Humans were afraid of the stupidest&nbsp;
things. SCP-682 thought to itself.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:03.420
It waited in this white room for&nbsp;
what felt like several hours until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:06.660
it was eventually no-clipped back into Level 11.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:08.880
“RALPH!!!”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:15.480
SCP-682 roared, loud enough to shatter the glass&nbsp;
windows on several buildings in the infinite city.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:20.040
It charged out of the skyscraper and onto&nbsp;
the roof of a nearby apartment building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:23.340
which just so happened to be&nbsp;
another surface with no-clip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:28.200
capabilities. 682 never got to hear a&nbsp;
response back from the talk radio host&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:33.060
before it fell several stories down into&nbsp;
another level of The Backrooms entirely.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:37.980
Level 13: An apartment building&nbsp;
that, while not technically infinite,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:42.600
was presumed to have a very high&nbsp;
number of floors. The hallways were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:48.420
more cramped than the hotel on Level 5,&nbsp;
so SCP-682 shrunk itself a bit to avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:52.740
getting stuck. It gritted its teeth&nbsp;
and prepared for the usual routine.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:53.760
3…2…1…

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:01.380
A clump, a female moth, and a hound came slinking&nbsp;
down the hallway like a random encounter in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:08.640
JRPG. SCP-682 hated these Backrooms entities so&nbsp;
very much, and could barely fathom why they could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.320
stand each other. It seemed that no matter&nbsp;
what level these hostile entities appeared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:17.580
the goon squad only ever attacked creatures&nbsp;
that weren’t native to The Backrooms.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:21.480
Without further deliberation,&nbsp;
SCP-682 ran the Three Stooges over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:26.400
trampling them with its superior power.&nbsp;
It was more than done taking small fry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.180
seriously and that included Curly, Larry, and Moe.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:36.660
As it wandered through the halls, SCP-682 started&nbsp;
to hear the droning easy-listening music which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:41.460
pervaded this entire level. It was the sort&nbsp;
of sound that humans used in elevators and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:47.580
grocery stores, places where the dull mundanity&nbsp;
of life was meant to serve as a comfort. And yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:51.540
it seemed to be the soundtrack of&nbsp;
The Backrooms latest hellish level.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:55.800
In a way, SCP-682 started to feel&nbsp;
pity for the humans trapped here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:00.600
not because their suffering was a bad thing from&nbsp;
its perspective, but because of the fragility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:06.120
of their finite psyches. If whatever force&nbsp;
that created The Backrooms did intend it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:11.880
be a realm that tormented humans, the humans&nbsp;
were definitely making it too easy. And if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:17.040
humans themselves made this to contain other&nbsp;
humans, the implications were even sillier.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:20.400
When the very structures that humans&nbsp;
built to shelter themselves from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:25.500
elements - apartment buildings, cities, towns&nbsp;
- were able to cause this much fear in them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:31.080
it was a sure sign that humanity was always doomed&nbsp;
to retreat screaming back into the wilderness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:36.960
after centuries of learning nothing from its&nbsp;
collective delusion of civilization. Or at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:43.020
least they would be doomed to that fate, if they&nbsp;
weren’t already doomed to be wiped out by SCP-682.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:46.020
Just like every entity in The Backrooms.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:51.900
682 wouldn’t rest until every last faceling,&nbsp;
clump, death moth, death rat, smiler, hound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:56.280
duller, burster, and any other ridiculous&nbsp;
entity that dared to crawl through these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.280 --> 00:15:01.680
wretched corridors was personally sent to its&nbsp;
end. It got so pumped up thinking about this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:07.200
that it didn’t even notice itself no-clipping&nbsp;
again. Thousands of floors rushed by in the blink&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:11.820
of a moment until the reptile finally dropped&nbsp;
through the lobby of the apartment building.

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:15.000
A new level unlocked! Just like that!

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:19.920
SCP-682 regained its bearings on&nbsp;
a forest floor covered in vibrant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:23.100
crimson grass. The trees had pitch-black bark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:29.280
almost blending in with the night itself. The&nbsp;
sky above was a glistening sea of bright stars.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:35.760
This was level 14 - known to most explorers&nbsp;
as Paradise. This level had a strange power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:41.400
which supposedly made the explorer happy and&nbsp;
feeling as though they belonged. However much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:45.960
like the darkness within the suburbs, Level&nbsp;
14’s happiness-inducing atmosphere would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:49.500
have the opposite effect on&nbsp;
the hard-to-destroy reptile.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:53.760
It hated this forest even more than&nbsp;
any previous level of the backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:58.800
and wanted out immediately. From&nbsp;
experience, 682 knew that poking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:02.220
around would eventually result in it&nbsp;
finding the entrance to the next level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:07.380
so it high-tailed its way through the trees.&nbsp;
It needed to find that exit desperately.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:12.300
As it ran through the woods, 682 could&nbsp;
hear howling somewhere far in the distance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:16.440
and it didn’t sound like a pack&nbsp;
of wild animals. Disturbingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:21.000
it sounded like a crowd of humans attempting&nbsp;
noises similar to wolves, but they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:26.040
committing so much to the performance that it&nbsp;
almost seemed like they truly believed they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:32.400
were wolves. Whatever hippy-dippy nonsense&nbsp;
was going on here wasn’t SCP-682’s concern.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:38.520
Right now, it was burning with so much contempt&nbsp;
for Level 14 that it could barely think straight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:44.400
Its feet crashed through a field of pale-white&nbsp;
bones, lying just beneath the grass, but it kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:50.580
on running. It collided with a tree, downing&nbsp;
it in a second, but it just kept running. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:57.060
howling ceased in the distance, and still, SCP-682&nbsp;
continued to run as fast and as far as it could.

00:16:57.060 --> 00:17:00.960
Then, against all odds, the&nbsp;
creature's own mind began to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:05.220
turn against it as the effect of&nbsp;
Level 14 continued to take hold.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:09.540
You don’t belong anywhere.&nbsp;
You are a mistake of nature.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:14.700
SCP-682 could recognize its own&nbsp;
voice echoing in its head and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.880
for the first time, it was terrified of itself.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:21.900
You are a thing that cannot ever be happy. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:27.540
paradise will never accept you.&nbsp;
Nowhere will ever accept you.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:31.380
You are… disgusting.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:38.340
SCP-682 froze in its tracks. There was&nbsp;
no exit from this place. The Backrooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:43.260
had won the sick game it was playing with the&nbsp;
reptile’s existence. It would be trapped here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:49.620
forever in this inverted Paradise for humans: a&nbsp;
self-loathing immortal without any hope of escape.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:55.260
It was so paralyzed by the immense disgust that&nbsp;
it felt for itself that it almost didn’t notice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.260 --> 00:18:00.660
a speck of blue among all the red: the&nbsp;
blue on the feathers of a hyacinth macaw.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:04.140
“Jerry?” SCP-682 said aloud.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:11.040
Don’t follow him. You are a monster. You&nbsp;
will never know companionship or love.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:16.800
“Shut up, you disgusting creature!”&nbsp;
SCP-682 growled back at its own mind.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:21.300
Shakily, it began to move its legs in&nbsp;
the direction of Jerry. The bird-like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:25.860
entity was the only thing that still&nbsp;
felt real about Level 14. Everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:30.840
practically faded away into a churning&nbsp;
ocean of red and black. It took every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:35.940
ounce of willpower that SCP-682 had,&nbsp;
but it kept moving towards Jerry.

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:40.380
You are the disgusting monster&nbsp;
to ever exist. The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:48.120
should have destroyed you. The Backrooms will&nbsp;
destroy you. You don’t belong in this world.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:54.060
SCP-682 did everything it could to shut out&nbsp;
the voice, even as Jerry took off and flew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.060 --> 00:19:00.480
deeper into the crimson forests of Level 14.&nbsp;
Without even realizing, 682 had grown a pair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:05.340
of blue wings of its own. It followed Jerry&nbsp;
through the trees and then higher towards the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:12.060
starry sky. One thought cut all the negativity&nbsp;
that had been swirling through SCP-682’s mind.

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:18.120
It doesn’t matter if I don’t belong&nbsp;
anywhere else. Jerry is all I need.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:25.560
A light shone down from above, and suddenly it&nbsp;
was as if Level 14 itself was rejecting SCP-682.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:31.620
While the reptile was focused on Jerry, a piece&nbsp;
of the sky seemed to glitch, and then - as if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:36.600
it were a solid piece of machinery - it&nbsp;
fell down towards the red grass below.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:41.820
Behind the fallen chunk of sky was a metallic&nbsp;
hallway, not unlike some of those back at The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:48.120
Foundation. Jerry flew through the opening, and&nbsp;
SCP-682 followed with its own macaw-like feathered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:54.540
wings. A shift in gravity, much like the event&nbsp;
on level 7 occurred, and 682 soon found itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:59.700
standing inside of the long silvery corridor,&nbsp;
having come through a hole in the ceiling.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:01.440
Goodbye, Level 14.

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:05.640
Hello, Level 15 - The Futuristic Hallways.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.880
Aww yeah! The Future Rules!

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:14.640
Here we are in the future, and it's right! It&nbsp;
was certainly a lot less of a personal nightmare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:21.720
to SCP-682. Jerry had clearly flown ahead, but&nbsp;
682 knew somewhere deep down that it wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:26.460
have made it here without him. If the reptile&nbsp;
had any respect for the concept of fairness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:32.160
it’d probably consider the debt for Jerry fleeing&nbsp;
in Level 10 to be repaid. But its empathy wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:36.960
quite so sophisticated that it could&nbsp;
weigh favors like that so it soldiered on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:42.480
looking to catch up with Jerry for no&nbsp;
particular reason. At least as far as it knew.

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:47.580
The hallways were definitely manmade in&nbsp;
appearance, but from a time so technologically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:51.960
advanced that even The Foundation couldn’t&nbsp;
dream of it. The best part about level 15&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:57.000
was that it was filled with what appeared to&nbsp;
be human remains. Most of these corpses were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:02.700
marked with knife and gunshot wounds, perhaps the&nbsp;
result of some kind of mass-slaughter. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.900
it was clear that all of these&nbsp;
humans had been dead for a long time.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:12.780
The only good human is a dead&nbsp;
human. SCP-682 mused to itself.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:18.840
It seemed that the future did in fact&nbsp;
kinda rule, because from 682’s perspective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:25.140
Level 15 was populated entirely by “good&nbsp;
humans.” There was still no sign of Jerry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:31.020
but there were also no annoying entities to&nbsp;
waste the reptile’s time. Compared to Level 14,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:34.500
the futuristic hallways were the real paradise.

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:39.540
While it was as far away as ever from&nbsp;
feeling any kind of authentic contentment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:44.400
SCP-682 decided that this place was acceptable.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:49.680
No life. No Foundation. I’m&nbsp;
starting to like it here.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:56.220
Now go check out “Could SCP-682 be Contained&nbsp;
in the Backrooms?” and “SCP-682 Slaughters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:56.220 --> 00:22:00.660
Through the Backrooms” for more of the Hard&nbsp;
to Destroy Lizard wrecking this liminal hell!

